---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
const EMAIL = 'tyler@btso.dev';
---
<Legal
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy | Chart107: Part 107 Test Prep"
  heading="Chart107 privacy"
  description="What Chart107 keeps on your device, what it sends, and what it never does."
  lastUpdated="November 24, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Chart107 is an offline FAA Part 107 Remote Pilot study app for iPhone, Android and the web.
    It has no user accounts, no ads, no third-party analytics and no cross-app tracking.
    Chart107 uses public-domain FAA materials from faa.gov and is not affiliated with or endorsed
    by the Federal Aviation Administration.
  </p>

  <h2>Your study progress stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your answered questions, spaced-repetition intervals, completed sectional chart lessons,
    mastered flashcards, mock exam history, exam date target and theme preference are stored
    locally on your device (SQLite on iOS and Android, localStorage in the web demo). We do not
    operate a backend server and do not upload your study data anywhere. If your phone backs up
    app data to iCloud or Google Backup, Apple or Google handles those backups under your account.
  </p>

  <h2>One-time Pro purchase</h2>
  <p>
    Chart107 offers a single optional one-time in-app purchase to unlock all 12 FAA sectional chart
    lessons, 480 source-cited questions, 40 flashcards and unlimited practice exams. Payment is
    handled by the Apple App Store or Google Play; we never see your card or payment details.
    To verify and restore your purchase across reinstalls, the app uses
    <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat</a>, which receives a random anonymous
    app user ID generated on your device, your purchase receipt and basic technical details such as
    app version, device type and store storefront. This information is used solely to unlock and
    restore your purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional live airport weather lookup</h2>
  <p>
    Inside the METAR trainer on iOS and Android, you can optionally type an airport ICAO code (such
    as KDEN) and tap Decode Live to fetch the current public METAR directly from the National Weather
    Service Aviation Weather Center (<a href="https://aviationweather.gov">aviationweather.gov</a>).
    No personal data or location is sent; only the 4-letter station code you entered is requested.
    All 6 bundled METAR drills and every chart lesson work 100% offline without making any network
    requests.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share your information, show advertisements, embed ad SDKs or third-party
    analytics, track you across apps or websites, or collect your name, email address, contacts,
    location, photos or microphone.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Chart107 is intended for prospective FAA Remote Pilots (minimum age 14 to take the FAA Part 107
    knowledge test) and does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear all local study progress anytime from Readiness &rarr; Reset Study Progress, or by
    uninstalling the app. To request deletion of anonymous purchase records held by RevenueCat, email
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. Your Apple or Google store account retains its own
    purchase history.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page will be updated. Questions or support
    requests can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
